\section{Automated Error Handling \& Self-Healing Protocol}

\subsection{Recovery Sequence}

\paragraph{1. CFL Violation Interception}
If
\[
\frac{v_{\max}\Delta t}{\Delta x}
+
2\frac{D_{\max}\Delta t}{(\Delta x)^2}
> 1,
\]
local integration timesteps are compressed:
\[
\Delta t \leftarrow \frac{\Delta t}{2}.
\]

\paragraph{2. Stiff Matrix Solver Redirection}
Stiff subsystems automatically pivot from explicit Runge--Kutta schemes to implicit BDF solvers to maintain convergence through severe nonlinear discontinuities.

\paragraph{3. Dissipative Energy Injection}
The Hamiltonian damping term is scaled upward:
\[
\gamma \leftarrow \gamma_{\mathrm{new}} > \gamma_{\mathrm{old}},
\]
bleeding artificial kinetic energy spikes and forcing trajectories back into the Lyapunov-stable basin of attraction.